        "text": "You are applying two focused review fixes to `src/server/storage/dbm/operations.py` in the Talium code-econ storage module. Work from `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ`. Canonical interpreter: **`venv/bin/python`**.\n\n## Fix 1 (correctness): stamp Alembic to head on force-recreate\nIn `operations.py`, the `init(cfg, force=False)` function's `force` branch currently does `Base.metadata.drop_all(eng)` then `Base.metadata.create_all(eng)` and returns `\"recreated\"`. Problem: when phase-2 migration files exist, a force-recreate leaves the `alembic_version` table empty while the schema is actually at head — so `status()` misreports and a later `migrate()` would try to re-apply migrations.\nFix: in the `force` branch, AFTER `create_all`, add:\n```python\n    if _has_migrations():\n        command.stamp(alembic_config(cfg), \"head\")\n```\n(so the DB is marked at head, consistent with the freshly-created schema). `command` is already imported from `alembic`. Keep the `return \"recreated\"`.\n\n## Fix 2 (honest deferral): TODO for admin_dsn DB/role creation\nstorage.md §6 says `init` (absent-DB case) should create the database/role if needed using `cfg.admin_dsn`. This is not implemented. Add a TODO comment (per the repo's TODO convention) at the start of `init`, e.g.:\n```python\n    # TODO(storage): create database/role if absent using cfg.admin_dsn (storage.md §6).\n    # Deferred: db-core/role provisioning is a separate concern; init currently assumes\n    # the database and role already exist.\n```\nDo NOT implement the actual provisioning — just the TODO marker so it isn't silently lost.\n\n## Constraints\n- Change ONLY `src/server/storage/dbm/operations.py`. No \"Claude\" anywhere.\n- These paths are DB-only (tests skip without TALIUM_TEST_DSN), so you cannot add a passing DB test — that's fine; do NOT add a test that would error.\n\n## Verify & commit\nRun `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/ -q` (expect: same as before — prior passes + operations tests skip, 0 failed) and `venv/bin/python -c \"from server.storage.dbm import operations; print('ok')\"`. Commit with message: `fix(storage): stamp head on force-recreate; TODO for admin_dsn provisioning`.\n\n## Report\nAppend to `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-9-report.md` under \"## Fix round\": both changes, the test command + result, the import check. Reply with ONLY: Status, commit SHA + subject, one-line test result, report path.",
